WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:06.880
OK, we now have just one week and one day from&nbsp;
the election. Three different models to look at.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:11.120
Every model says the same thing. And people&nbsp;
emailed me over the weekend saying, David,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:16.960
you've got to comment on these models because is&nbsp;
there any case to be made for anything other than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:23.133
Biden crushing Trump? So let's look at the models.&nbsp;
And yes, every single one of these says Joe Biden,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.133 --> 00:00:28.080
is doing really well. The first model is the&nbsp;
538 model, which currently says that Joe Biden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:34.640
has an 87 percent chance to win. While Trump has a&nbsp;
12 percent chance to win with a one percent chance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:41.840
that neither candidate gets to 270 electoral&nbsp;
votes. This means if you run 100 simulations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:47.600
with the current polling inputs and you adjust&nbsp;
for margin for error, Biden would win in 87&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:53.520
simulations and Trump would win in 12th. If you&nbsp;
look at the electoral vote projections of 538,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:57.840
Joe Biden, they believe, will end up with&nbsp;
three hundred and forty five electoral votes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:04.640
Trump with not even 200. That would be a very&nbsp;
solid win for Joe. And then lastly, looking at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:10.880
popular vote predictions, 538 estimates that&nbsp;
Biden will win about 53 percent of the popular&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:17.520
vote with a roughly eight point margin. That&nbsp;
would be the largest popular vote victory in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:23.280
very long time. And then if you look at the model&nbsp;
from the economists, the economists estimate is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:30.320
that Joe Biden has a 95 percent chance to win the&nbsp;
electoral vote in terms of the popular vote. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:37.440
Economist says Biden has a greater than 99 percent&nbsp;
chance of winning the popular vote and cites&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:44.320
some popular or rather electoral vote numbers&nbsp;
which give a possibility that Trump wins&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:51.680
but overwhelmingly skew to Joe Biden in terms&nbsp;
of the Electoral College. As far as their best&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:57.120
guess on electoral numbers, it's not a range here,&nbsp;
but a best guess. The Economist believes that it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:08.560
will be Biden 352 and Trump 186, which also would&nbsp;
be a huge win for for Joe Biden. And then lastly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:15.520
the in terms of the electoral vote trends, The&nbsp;
Economist has seen Biden's expected electoral&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:20.160
votes rising for the last roughly two months&nbsp;
since the start of September. And then we've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:27.040
got the Princeton model run run by Sam Wang.&nbsp;
The estimate is Biden three six, the electoral&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:34.880
votes with the Senate going to Democrats 52 to&nbsp;
48 and Democrats keeping control of the House.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:39.440
So what's the counter to all this? Because&nbsp;
it all just looks so great, right? Record&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:45.040
early voting more Democrats than Republicans&nbsp;
in some states. It just looks great. Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:51.040
the counterpoints are number one. None of this can&nbsp;
account for voter suppression, and that could be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:57.040
a big factor. Period. Don't even need to say&nbsp;
more. That's just huge by itself. Number two,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:04.240
the polling looking at people who have not yet&nbsp;
voted but are likely to vote is overwhelmingly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:10.800
in favor of Trump in some of these battleground&nbsp;
states, suggesting that, yes, the. Early voting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:16.720
may well favor Biden in some of these key states,&nbsp;
but the people who will vote on Election Day&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:23.840
may heavily favor Donald Trump. So what can&nbsp;
we do? All we can do is vote. You know it.&nbsp;

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:29.520
I know it. We've got eight days to go. Let&nbsp;
me know your voting plan. I'm on Twitter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:34.240
at David Pakman. And we will have much more on&nbsp;
this coming up a little bit later in the show.

